        "id": 87360,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-25T22:20:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Pandora's moon isn't so much broken as covered in fiery-looking cracks and craters and stuff, as far as I can tell (nearly done with the final DLC on Normal Mode in Borderlands 2, have been playing for a month or so now).</p><p>I saw the first part of a film recently in which the intro described how some kind of alien race invaded Earth and shattered the Moon (basically breaking it into many pieces which remained fairly close together, not scattered throughout the sky or raining down onto the planet or off into space or anything like that), which for some reason caused Earth to almost immediately. have loads of catastrophic disasters, possibly involving tides or something. What.</p>",
        "post_number": 74,
